    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2Mv6egQG3L1RGxtCNMQuupj)_\n\nWhen `sp-split-leave-parents` turns a heading into a file title, any `[[id:...][...]]` links in the heading are removed from the title and listed in a `- seealso :: ...` meta line in the body of the new note (new option `sp-split-links-to-seealso`, default on).\n\n- `sp-split--extract-id-links` and `sp-split--body-with-seealso` are called from the existing write-file advice, so it runs automatically. An existing `seealso` line is extended without duplicates; if the heading is only links, the title falls back to their descriptions.\n- Doc (`sp-org-lint.org`) and tangled `.el` changed together; new tests `tests/sp-split-leave-parents-test.el` (7 tests pass in Emacs 29 batch with Vulpea/Denote stubbed). Tangle check shows no drift for this module.\n- Not run against real Vulpea: I could not see `vulpea-split--write-file`, so I assumed its TITLE argument is the heading text including links.\n- Branch name is the session's `claude/project-thread-ilz734`, not number-prefixed (the PR number was not known beforehand).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiASw5V8hj46NAkBiKS)_",
